 "_doc": "The Kraken (Pontoppidan, 1752-53): a sea-beast so vast that its back, rising out of the sea, was taken for a cluster of small islands, its arms like the masts of ships, able to pull down the greatest ship. A great mottled mantle rising from the sea with a huge golden eye, long thick arms rising high out of the water and curling over at their tips, pale suckers along them, and the sea foaming round it. Built by tools/art/build_gears.py.",
